course: dictionary
lesson: 10596
title: Understandable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Understandable» comes from «understand». It has two meanings. First, it means easy to understand, or clear: instructions that are understandable can be followed without confusion.
explain: Second, it means normal or reasonable in that situation, so you can see why someone feels or acts that way. «It is understandable that you're upset» does not say you were wrong to feel upset. It says the feeling makes sense.
explain: Use the words around it to pick the right meaning. In «Sulking after a fair consequence is understandable, but it does not put things right», the sentence says the feeling makes sense, but sulking still does not fix the problem.
fact: Understandable means easy to understand, or clear.
fact: Understandable also means normal or reasonable, so you can see why someone feels or acts that way.
fact: «Feeling angry at the tablet, the channel or the friend who showed it is understandable; the screen did something you didn't choose.»
fact: «People lie for understandable reasons: to escape trouble, to be admired, to get something they want, or to cover for a friend.»
fact: Useful phrases include «perfectly understandable», «it is understandable that» and «easy to understand».
exercise: «The map was understandable, so we found the café in minutes.» What does understandable mean here? | Hard to read and confusing | Very old | *Easy to understand and clear | Expensive
exercise: «Feeling upset after losing the match is understandable.» What does this tell you? | Losing matches is never allowed | The match was cancelled | You were wrong to feel upset | *Your feeling makes sense
exercise: Choose the word that fits the gap: «He lied to cover for his friend, which is ____, though it was still wrong.» | Curt | *Understandable | Barely | Ancient
test: «The instructions were so understandable that even Mia could build the shelf.» What does understandable mean? | Hard to read | Loud | Very old | *Clear and easy to follow
test: «It is understandable that you feel nervous before a big test.» What does understandable mean here? | Silly to feel nervous | *Normal, so the feeling makes sense | Impossible | Not allowed
exam: «Reasons should be understandable to people of any faith or none.» Which meaning fits best? | Reasons are very long | Reasons must be kept secret | Reasons are always wrong | *Reasons can be clearly understood and seen as sensible by everyone
